    "result_text": "The build is green. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required emitting an immutable structured `AUDIT` event `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event:'OWNER_CREATED'}` alongside the existing audit line, with `seq` monotonic across creates and the event carrying the owner's *current primary identifier*.\n\n**Change** \u2014 one file, one already-trivial method (`SaveOwner.service`, CC 1, no sibling methods, so `WMC_other` is 0):\n\n- Added a `static final AtomicInteger EVENT_SEQ` for the cross-create monotonic sequence.\n- Hoisted `membershipLevel` into a local (computed once, shared by both log lines).\n- Introduced `String primaryId = owner.getCustomerCode()` \u2014 the \"current primary identifier\" seam, so the future customerCode\u2192memberId unification is a one-line swap rather than a rework.\n- Emitted the JSON event via the `AUDIT` logger. SLF4J only treats the empty `{}` token as a placeholder, so the literal JSON braces (`{\"seq\":\u2026}`) pass through untouched.\n\n**Why this shape:** adding a dedicated pipeline step + YAML wiring would touch two files and, per the cost model, multiply the whole cost by 2. Extending `SaveOwner` in place keeps it at a single file over the simplest method in the module \u2014 the lowest structural impact available. The event is immutable (a log record) and the sequence is process-wide.\n\n`AcceptanceTest` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`), and the emitted line confirms the format:\n`{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`",
